<title>PERU: Korea Ex-Im bank in credit pact with Peru's Wiese.</title>
<headline>Korea Ex-Im bank in credit pact with Peru's Wiese.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Export-Import Bank on Friday signed a pact extending a $15 million credit line to Peru's second largest bank, Banco Wiese, for imports from South Korea, Banco Wiese said.</p>
<p>&quot;It is the first time that this Korean bank has given a credit line to a private Peruvian financial institution, which shows the recovery of confidence in the country and the leadership that Banco Wiese has been developing,&quot; Banco Wiese said.  </p>
<p>Banco Wiese officials said the 10-year credit would be used primarily for imports of raw materials, semi-manufactured goods, consumer goods, parts and components, industrial plants and other capital goods.</p>
<p>The signing of the pact coincided with the visit to Peru of South Korean President Kim Young-sam.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima Newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
